     You can't rule out #1 unless you know that milky potions
in the current game have a type which monsters never drink.  I
suspect that some monster attempted to drink such a potion--once
you were sufficiently close, but not necessarily in view--and
released a ghost instead of receiving the potion's benefit.

     The types monsters will drink when not yet wounded are
gain level, invisibility, speed, and polymorph.  (The last will
only be used by wimpy monsters; strong ones won't risk becoming
weaker.  Invisibility won't be used by peaceful monsters unless
you can see invisible.)  Even if you hadn't dished out any remote
damage via ranged attacks, monsters might have injured themselves
via traps.  So add healing, extra healing, and full healing to
the list of potions monsters might have drunk out of your view.
If any on the list has description "milky", we have a plausible
explanation....


